                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13166.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-12T09:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 12, 1914, 9 a.m. No.
                        3</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s message for Zapata, September 7. The attempts to come to some
                    agreement with Zapata without the assistance of the United States, though
                    repeatedly suggested, have resulted in total failure and increased friction. In
                    fact actual fighting has occurred at several places. The Department’s
                    instructions concerning the President’s wishes will not be overlooked and
                    opportunity will be sought to bring the two parties into agreement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
